{
 "protocol": "scripts/bench_serve.py: served models streamed in 20 ms blocks through serve.Session in process, as fast as the CPU allows, 2 torch threads, via scripts/dev/gate.sh (nice 5). RTF = processing wall / audio; cpu_rtf = process CPU time / audio (both threads). Per-component sums are the Session's own timers (asr = feed_frames: mel + encoder + RNNT + VAD head; turn = speaker-conditioned encoder pass + turn head; diar = StreamingDiarizer.feed). 'components' installs leaf timers (ms per 160 ms of audio). 'ab' interleaves two engines per clip so both see the same machine load; 'compare' checks protocol-message equality. load_* = 1/5/15 min load averages, swap_used_mb = macOS swap at the end of the run: the machine was shared with other agents' jobs throughout (load 4-10), so wall figures are upper bounds; ratios within one 'ab' run are the fair comparison.",
